Package: MEXGB
Type: Package
Title: Mixed-Effect Extreme Gradient Boosting for Longitudinal Data
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(person("Ajibade Kunle", "Saheed", role = "aut"),
             person("Oyebayo Ridwan", "Olaniran", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                    email = "olaniran.or@kwasu.edu.ng"),
             person("Mohd Asrul Affendi", "Abdullah", role = "aut"),
             person("Saidat Fehintola", "Olaniran", role = "ctb",
                    comment = "Co-author of MEGB, from which Gaussian update code was adapted"))
Maintainer: Oyebayo Ridwan Olaniran <olaniran.or@kwasu.edu.ng>
Description: Fits mixed-effects extreme gradient boosting models for Gaussian,
    binary and clustered right-censored survival outcomes. Combines subject-specific
    random effects with boosted trees and optional penalised linear terms using
    'xgboost' and 'glmnet'. Provides within-subject cross-fitting, predictor screening,
    approximate variance-component estimation, conditional prediction and simulation
    utilities. Builds on extreme gradient boosting by Chen and Guestrin (2016)
    <doi:10.1145/2939672.2939785> and mixed-effects tree ensembles by
    Capitaine et al. (2021) <doi:10.1177/0962280220946080>.
